  "abstract": "The Bullet Cluster (1E 0657-56) is re-examined under Energy-Flow Cosmology (EFC) in light of three JWST-era studies (Cha et al. 2025, Rihtarsic et al. 2026, Cho et al. 2025) providing the highest-resolution mass map, the first spectroscopically anchored parametric lens model, and the definitive ~10:1 minor merger mass ratio. We confront these results with EFC across four axes: (i) cluster merger geometry structural constraint under the revised mass ratio; (ii) the pre-registered A_sig directional lensing residual estimator; (iii) the tightened SIDM bound sigma/m < 0.5 cm^2 g^-1 within EFC's no-particle ontology; (iv) qualitative confrontation of the regime-transition prediction (mu ~ 1.1, Sigma ~ 1.2 at cluster scales). All three studies are consistent with EFC's structural predictions; the 10:1 ratio simplifies the geometric exclusion argument. A PIEMD A_sig 2D baseline yields A_sig = -6.9e-4, p = 0.98, validating the test operator (not the physical hypothesis). The pre-registered A_sig test on the free-form delta_kappa = kappa_obs - kappa_PIEMD residual remains the only observable capable of directly discriminating between EFC and LCDM at this scale. No new parameters are introduced.",
  "sameAs": "https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.31963668",
  "doi": "10.6084/m9.figshare.31963668"
